01:20:20.448 --> 01:20:24.948
The families of Musaceae are native to Asia, Africa, and the Pacific.

01:20:25.248 --> 01:20:28.438
They're closest related to plants like heliconias and gingers.

01:20:28.448 --> 01:20:32.468
They're not actually trees. They're called trees a lot, but it's not true.

01:20:32.688 --> 01:20:34.998
They're really soft, fleshy plants.

01:20:35.008 --> 01:20:38.438
And when you grow them, they're more akin to growing like a vegetable actually than any

01:20:38.448 --> 01:20:42.310
true fruit tree. So first genus called Inceti.

01:20:42.320 --> 01:20:43.830
There's about eight species recognized.

01:20:43.840 --> 01:20:45.590
They're native to Asia and Africa.

01:20:45.600 --> 01:20:48.470
They only flower once and then completely die.

01:20:48.480 --> 01:20:50.950
They have a very interesting form to them.

01:20:50.960 --> 01:20:55.430
They don't look like typical banana plants if you're used to seeing common banana plants

01:20:55.440 --> 01:20:59.430
on a farm. There are some varieties that are really ornamental.

01:20:59.440 --> 01:21:04.150
And so you'll see them as landscape ornamental plants throughout even places like

01:21:04.160 --> 01:21:05.606
New York in the summer.

01:21:06.000 --> 01:21:10.470
There's also a domesticated form of one of these Nceti called Enset, specifically the

01:21:10.480 --> 01:21:15.190
species Nceti ventricosum that is used as an edible crop in Ethiopia, but it's not for

01:21:15.200 --> 01:21:19.590
the fruit. It's actually for the starch in the underground parts and in the stem of the

01:21:19.600 --> 01:21:20.280
plant.

01:21:21.024 --> 01:21:24.534
This is Inceti superbum, native to India and Thailand.

01:21:24.544 --> 01:21:29.254
Just a fun little weird plant if it's grown in a container, but it also gets massive.

01:21:29.264 --> 01:21:33.894
This plant on the right, you can't really tell the scale, but at the good 25 feet tall,

01:21:33.904 --> 01:21:37.894
they have these big wide stems at the bottom and they shoot their bunches really high

01:21:37.904 --> 01:21:41.190
into the air, giving kind of funky, weird look to them.

01:21:42.000 --> 01:21:45.990
There's also inceti glaucum, which is native all over Southeast Asia.

01:21:46.000 --> 01:21:47.830
The seeds are used medicinally.

01:21:47.840 --> 01:21:50.230
The plants are used as animal feed.

